    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "req_ids": [
        "R3"
      ],
      "problem_type": "implementation",
      "detail": "The precedence constraint is implemented with reversed direction. The code uses `start[u] >= start[v] + proc[v]` for `(u, v) = (J1, J3)`, which enforces J1 starts after J3 finishes. The requirement is J1 finishes before J3 starts (`start[J1] + proc[J1] <= start[J3]`).",
      "evidence_level": "llm_judgment",
      "status": "suspected",
      "proposed_checks": [
        "python3 -c \"import json, subprocess; p=subprocess.run(['python3','solve.py'],capture_output=True,text=True); d=json.load(open('solution.json')); j1=[j for j in d['jobs'] if j['job_id']=='J1'][0]; j3=[j for j in d['jobs'] if j['job_id']=='J3'][0]; assert j1['end'] <= j3['start'], f'Precedence violated: J1 end {j1[\\\"end\\\"]} > J3 start {j3[\\\"start\\\"]}'\"",
        "grep -n 'start\\[u\\] >= start\\[v\\]' solve.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "req_ids": [
        "R2"
      ],
      "problem_type": "implementation",
      "detail": "The no-overlap constraints use a big-M formulation that may allow overlapping intervals when jobs are on different machines or due to coefficient errors. Specifically, the coefficients in the big-M terms (3 and 2) need verification against the standard disjunctive programming formulation to ensure they correctly enforce non-overlap only when both jobs are on the same machine.",
      "evidence_level": "llm_judgment",
      "status": "suspected",
      "proposed_checks": [
        "python3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('solution.json') as f:\n    d = json.load(f)\njobs_by_m = {}\nfor j in d['jobs']:\n    m = j['machine']\n    if m not in jobs_by_m:\n        jobs_by_m[m] = []\n    jobs_by_m[m].append(j)\nfor m, js in jobs_by_m.items():\n    js.sort(key=lambda x: x['start'])\n    for i in range(len(js)-1):\n        if js[i]['end'] > js[i+1]['start']:\n            raise AssertionError(f'Overlap on {m}: {js[i][\\\"job_id\\\"]} ends at {js[i][\\\"end\\\"]}, {js[i+1][\\\"job_id\\\"]} starts at {js[i+1][\\\"start\\\"]}')\nprint('No overlaps found')\n\""
      ]
    }
  ]
}
